<title>ITALY: Banca Roma net profit 103.2bln lire in 96.</title>
<headline>Banca Roma net profit 103.2bln lire in 96.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31.</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Parent net profit	 103.17 vs  88.29</p>
<p>    Pretax profit	     175.17 vs 144.29</p>
<p>    Gross loss		  107.39 vs (99.96 profit)</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries	   282.57 vs  44.33</p>
<p>Note - Banca di Roma said among the extraordinary items were some 154 billion lire raised by selling its stake in Pronto Italia and a further 117 billion lire raised by selling property assets.  </p>
<p>    Interest margin	  3,369.30 vs 3,223.92</p>
<p>Gross operating result 1,412.01 vs 1,173.46</p>
<p>    Admin costs		3,434.31 vs 3,313.08</p>
<p>    Client deposits	 71,000.00 vs n/g</p>
<p>    Client loans	    80,400.00 vs n/g</p>
<p>    Total loans	    107,700.00 vs n/g</p>
<p>Note: Banca di Roma said in a statement that bad or doubtful loans represented 9.4 percent of client loans. -- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
